    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298-a6">

                <pb facs="0787" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg665"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 27 Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Rosales to Mr. Pierce.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Matanzas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 13,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In answer to a communication which in the name of Messrs. Bea, Bellido &amp; Co.
                    you addressed me yesterday, requesting the suspension of the payment of the $800
                    fine imposed on the captain of the American steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Manhattan</hi> for deficiency of 4 tierces of lard on discharge of her trip
                    of the 28th of July last past, I must inform you that it is impossible for this
                    office to grant your request. The penalty was imposed in accordance with
                    paragraph 13 of article 121 of the regulations, and this administration has no
                    power to derogate superior orders.</p>
                <p>May God keep you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Augusto de
                    Rosales.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
